    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • Ford Rolls Out the Ranger MS-RT Champion Edition: You Can Choose Any Color As Long as It Is Black\nLand Rover Introduces Defender Alasia Pack in Europe, But Its Defender 90 Model Loses an Iconic Item\n6 photos\nPhoto: Land Rover\nFor one reason or the other, Land Rover has decided to announce the new Alasia Pack for the Old Continent's markets in Spain first, and we almost missed it as it flew under the radar in Spanish.\nNo worries, we’re ready to rectify that potential omission and let you know that JLR is offering something new on the Land Rover Defender in Europe while at the same time taking something away from the smallest member of the family, the Defender 90. By the way, JLR now has dedicated media portals to more than two brands.\nThat’s because they recently segmented Land Rover into Range Rover, Defender , and Discovery, while Jaguar remains a singular brand. There are also portals for JLR Classic, which is where all the retro-modern action takes place. Then they hid the new Land Rover Defender Alasia Pack in the Spanish-speaking area…\nAnd that’s how we ended up almost missing the news. Anyway, as far as we can tell, since we’re not native Spanish speakers, the new Alasia Pack isn’t exclusive to Spain, and it will be offered throughout Europe, which is a good thing. The new style pack adds Cyprus Copper accents to the exterior, aiming to provide the British off-roader with a touch of elegance without actually taking way any of its off-road chops.\nThe styling setup is offered on all versions, like the Defender 90, 100, and 130, and has a Mediterranean-inspired finish focused on Cyprus - Alasia was the island's ancient name, and the metal has historical importance to the island of Cyprus, once shaping entire early civilizations. Now, the copper finish appears on the outside on the front grille bar, on the side vents, and the rear towing eyes. It's a subtle makeover, indeed.\nThe Alasia Pack is now available to order across Europe for the Defender 90, 110, and 130, but Land Rover hasn’t announced any pricing details. This option does join the brand's growing range of customization choices, and if that’s not enough, it turns out that the small Defender 90 can now loose on of its defining exterior traits: the giant spare wheel sitting on its rear door.\nYep, as it turns out, instead of giving you something, Land Rover is taking away a feature – it’s all in the name of safety, as it allegedly improves rear visibility for the smallest member of the family. So, there’s now a spare wheel removal kit up for order in Europe, which takes away one of the SUV’s defining features for additional visibility and easier maneuvering in tight spaces.\nLand Rover didn’t even bother to design a separate fifth door without spare-wheel mounting points, but that would've added cost issues – now you’ll be stuck with your friends worrying that someone stole the spare wheel off your precious Defender 90, probably…\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nLand Rover Defender Alasia Pack Land Rover Defender land rover Defender Alasia Pack defender 90 spare wheel removal kit Europe\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Royal Enfield Hypershift Classic 650 Morphs Into a Tribute to Past Motorcycle Colors",
